{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Salesforce Omni-Channel routing readiness versus Case lifecycle alerts",
  "slug": "salesforce-omni-channel-routing-readiness-versus-case-lifecycle-alerts",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3adb007f5cba1fc50fa316ea0d1c01c93b1bd7436c0725efd0bb36384500132",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "e22f8bf19870ef1274760d3eb41a2fc99492738653b16a8ea104b2414a3b0ed3",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:9c4c5484a23c727ccf8d1b9e613b30aac6cbbad5e5798a9a497f11ff2b86ada7",
      "text": "Treat routing readiness as a separate condition from Case lifecycle alert eligibility. This is an architectural inference: Omni-Channel applies routing logic when work is assigned to an owner and does not reapply it after later field edits; PendingServiceRouting describes work waiting for routing or assignment. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/service/service-presence-developer-guide/guide/omnichannel-developer-guide-intro.html",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/object-reference/references/standard-objects/object-pendingservicerouting.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0884c6e012a9c6d8826c4e4915c19e01070ded0bfec4fd224e2252cd20248822",
        "ev:774f1fae08ec76bd100af66862ad225ee6c82dd840e16a00b108b5af5d7eea3a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:666a1fc49086ad72265c1a84f601a729d00500d818891aace17baa0166502e7a",
      "text": "For queue-based routing, PendingServiceRouting creation does not invoke before-insert or after-insert triggers, or actions such as triggers, workflow rules, or validation that could interfere with record creation. A design that expects an insert trigger on this routing record to deliver every alert conflicts with this documented behavior. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/object-reference/references/standard-objects/object-pendingservicerouting.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0c6a0bcbd202bbe773b9edd3b488d0e5fd1ba1a055cb3db668b3afb90791a40d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:a7e127a05d7f0241a02550b45bdd0cb9c0ab312746684d95916d63c482c6cba3",
      "text": "The routing object's readiness flag describes readiness to route work to an agent; when true, the PendingServiceRouting record cannot be edited. This is routing readiness, not evidence that a Case lifecycle alert has been delivered. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/object-reference/references/standard-objects/object-pendingservicerouting.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:24c5384cf13ce30b64fa5b7668b00c0aa8d7f28677eee23104a463a2b71417ba"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:b745b9ef658148424faf7274650102b13c981095debacaa79376d49878ca51fb",
      "text": "In a historical Stack Exchange report, a Case user said changing Status to Open or New did not resolve the reported routing-record creation failure. This is an attributed observation, not a verified current Salesforce defect. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://salesforce.stackexchange.com/questions/377548/field-integrity-exception-cant-create-pendingservicerouting-object-because-the/382112",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:e56ed06d8df9c62367d5e228d9cc41314a61ed1b5eed8dfa64334e905826341d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:d4b1af3bddddef956b17faf29897167a3b64c7dc811f664f7599d550e4ba80da",
      "text": "PendingServiceRouting readiness indicates whether a work item is ready to be routed to an agent; once true, the PendingServiceRouting record cannot be edited. It does not by itself attest that an agent has accepted the work. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/object-reference/references/standard-objects/object-pendingservicerouting.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:24c5384cf13ce30b64fa5b7668b00c0aa8d7f28677eee23104a463a2b71417ba"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:3c2e1f42a7d047fb23d3baafe0765859b2c5dbbacface4e7714df573f8b9cf8e",
      "text": "Do not interpret the routing-versus-lifecycle distinction as saying that work status never affects Omni-Channel. Status-based capacity measures accepted-work status, and optional capacity checks before reopening or reassigning work can reroute work when the rep lacks capacity. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.omnichannel_status_based_capacity.htm&language=en_US&type=5",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:8275e95a7170d45b8e1a571a25506a3e6b11df46ffd0a35a5ed484c52ef8241e",
        "ev:e78397594af46099ef1d1f15d8cd23df37d2ae651a819a2218577bfd22c9dc7f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:867055a332956fa13f1d3a376eecde413c30192192b5543375b236bbfa4e6a76",
      "text": "External-routing notifications have a routing-specific lifecycle: new work is sent to the partner application, which matches it to logged-in reps; Salesforce also notifies the partner after acceptance, decline, completion, and rep logout. These documented milestones should not be assumed to enumerate every later Case field change. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/service/service-presence-developer-guide/guide/omnichannel-external-routing-flow.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:3bc379be51ddb7ea0d083e94e0e2d16b5870543b8c901f252731c6a91b52d6e9"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "narrative": [
